This schema defines a JSON object representing a "Scene" in a multimedia presentation. A Scene contains a set of properties and Elements that can be shared among multiple Pages. Each Page can be associated with a Scene either explicitly by specifying the "scene" property or implicitly by using the default scene with the name "*". When a Page is associated with a Scene, it inherits all the properties from the Scene, including Elements. If the same property is specified in both the Page and the Scene, the value specified in the Page will be used. However, Elements will be deep-merged, meaning that Elements with an "id" property will be merged, and other Elements will be appended. Elements defined in the Scene are always placed below Elements specified in the Page.

Here is a JSON instance conforming to this schema:

```json
{
  "backgroundMusic": "background_music.mp3"
}
```

However, for a more complete example, let's consider a Scene with some properties and Elements:

```json
{
  "backgroundMusic": "background_music.mp3",
  "elements": {
    "header": {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Welcome to our presentation"
    },
    "footer": {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Thank you for watching"
    }
  }
}
```

This Scene defines a background music to be played when any Page associated with this Scene is active. It also defines two Elements, "header" and "footer", which can be used in Pages to display a welcome message and a thank you message, respectively

