- "mcversion" is a string representing the Minecraft version.
- "version" is a string representing the Forge version without the Minecraft version.
- "date" is a string representing the release date of the Forge version.
- "installer", "universal", "changelog", "mdk", "source", and "launcher" are ForgeDownload objects.
- "type" is a string representing the type of the Forge release. It can be "buggy", "common", "latest", or "recommended".

The ForgeDownload object has three properties: "md5", "sha1", and "path". "md5" and "sha1" are strings representing the MD5 and SHA1 checksums of the download, respectively. "path" is a string representing the URL path to concatenate with the Forge Maven URL.

