This JSON schema represents a formal specification for a Process and Content Network (PCN) model. The PCN model is a conceptual framework used to describe the structure and organization of a process or system. The schema defines three main components: domains, metadata, and steps.

The "domains" component is an array of objects, each representing a domain in the PCN model. Each domain object has three required properties: id, title, and subtitle.

The "metadata" component is an object that provides additional information about the PCN model. It has three properties: author, description, and title.

The "steps" component is an array of objects, each representing a step in the PCN model. Each step object has several required properties: id, title, type, and domain. The "domain" property references a domain object in the "domains" array. The "type" property specifies the type of step, which can be process, decision, wait, or divergent_process. The "domain" object also has a "region" property, which is an object with a "type" property that specifies the type of region and a "with_domain" property that references another domain object.

The "predecessors" property of the step object is an array of objects, each representing a predecessor step in the PCN model. Each predecessor object has three required properties: id, title, and type. The "type" property specifies the type of relationship between the step and its predecessor, which can be normal_relationship or loose_temporal_relationship.

The "problems" property of the step object is an array of objects, each representing a problem associated with the step. Each problem object has two required properties: description and type. The "type" property specifies the type of problem, which can be inconvenient, confusing, difficult, or likely_to_fail.

