This JSON schema describes a set of definitions related to OAuth 2.0 grant types. It defines four main types: "implicit", "authorization_code", "loginEndpoint", and "tokenRequestEndpoint".

The "implicit" grant type describes an endpoint for implicit grant, which is a flow that allows a client to obtain an access token without an additional access token request. It requires a "loginEndpoint" and an optional "tokenName".

The "authorization_code" grant type describes an endpoint for authorization code grant, which is a flow that involves the client redirecting the user to an authorization server, where the user grants access, and then the client exchanges the authorization code for an access token. It requires a "tokenEndpoint" and a "tokenRequestEndpoint".

The "loginEndpoint" defines a URL for the login endpoint, which is the endpoint that the user is redirected to when the client initiates the grant flow. It requires a "url" property.

The "tokenRequestEndpoint" defines a URL for the endpoint where the client exchanges the authorization code for an access token. It requires a "url", "clientIdName", and "clientSecretName" properties.

Here is a valid example of an object that conforms to this schema:

```json
