7. `id`: A unique identifier for the script.

8. `log`: An object with `quotes` and `text` properties. The `quotes` property is an array of quote objects that contain a `name`, `type`, and `value` properties. The `text` property is a string that represents the log message.

9. `name`: The name of the script.

10. `result`: An object with `bool` and `text` properties that indicate whether the script was successful or not. The `bool` property is a boolean value, and the `text` property is either "Success" or "Failure".

11. `signal_code`: The signal code of the script, which can be a number between 1 and 30 or null.

12. `strictness`: A boolean value that determines the strictness of the script.

13. `timeout`: The timeout value for the script in seconds.

14. `verbosity`: The verbosity level of the script, which can be a number between 0 and 5.

